From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: domicile CI <ci@domicile.invalid>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 07:42:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: a DRM window answers what startup asks it

`DrmWindowHost` `NOTREACHED()`s seven `PlatformWindow` methods, on a premise
stated in two of their comments: DRM does no scaling, so callers should always
use pixel bounds -- and by extension, nothing else on that list is ever asked
either.

That holds on ChromeOS, where `ash` never routes a window through
`DesktopWindowTreeHostPlatform`. It is false for a views browser on Linux,
which asks during startup: `WindowTreeHost::InitHost()` reaches
`DesktopWindowTreeHostPlatform::CalculateRootWindowBounds()`, which calls
`GetBoundsInDIP()`. Starting `chrome --ozone-platform=drm` dies there -- twenty
frames past the `CreateScreen()` that `DrmScreen` was added to answer.

Answering that one alone only moves the crash: `SizeConstraintsChanged()` is
next, from `DesktopNativeWidgetAura::InitNativeWidget()`, and the rest sit
behind ordinary window operations a running browser reaches. Stubbing all seven
is what gets the browser process past window creation and on to asking viz for
a root compositor frame sink, so the seven are taken together rather than one
crash at a time.

`HeadlessWindow` models every one of them, and these are its answers:

  * `Show`/`Hide`/`IsVisible` -- a `bool` the first two set and the third
    reads. A CRTC is always lit; what the browser is asking is what it last
    said, not what the hardware is doing.
  * `SetBoundsInDIP`/`GetBoundsInDIP` -- convert through the delegate, which is
    the only thing that knows a scale factor.
  * `SetRestoredBoundsInDIP`/`GetRestoredBoundsInDIP` -- store pixels, convert
    on the way in and out, and fall back to the current bounds, which is what a
    window that has never been maximised should restore to.
  * `SetWindowIcons` -- nothing draws a titlebar on a CRTC, so there is nowhere
    to put an icon.
  * `SizeConstraintsChanged` -- a window that fills a CRTC has no constraints
    to renegotiate.

The bounds conversions preserve upstream's behaviour wherever the old premise
genuinely held: `PlatformWindowDelegate::ConvertRectToDIP` is the identity, and
only `DesktopWindowTreeHostPlatform` -- the delegate the views browser supplies
-- overrides it with a real factor.

Every display `DrmScreen` reports has a device scale factor of 1 today, because
nothing sets one and a `DisplaySnapshot` does not carry one. So DIP and pixels
are the same number until that changes, and this is the identity in practice
rather than a conversion anybody can currently observe. It is written as the
conversion anyway: the identity is the delegate's answer, not an assumption
worth re-encoding here.
---
 ui/ozone/platform/drm/host/drm_window_host.cc | 38 +++++++++++++------
 ui/ozone/platform/drm/host/drm_window_host.h  |  7 ++++
 2 files changed, 34 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ui/ozone/platform/drm/host/drm_window_host.cc b/ui/ozone/platform/drm/host/drm_window_host.cc
index f31e0aa31a990..2585e47781d11 100644
--- a/ui/ozone/platform/drm/host/drm_window_host.cc
+++ b/ui/ozone/platform/drm/host/drm_window_host.cc
@@ -66,14 +66,18 @@ gfx::Rect DrmWindowHost::GetCursorConfinedBounds() const {
                                            : cursor_confined_bounds_;
 }
 
-void DrmWindowHost::Show(bool inactive) {}
+void DrmWindowHost::Show(bool inactive) {
+  visible_ = true;
+}
 
-void DrmWindowHost::Hide() {}
+void DrmWindowHost::Hide() {
+  visible_ = false;
+}
 
 void DrmWindowHost::Close() {}
 
 bool DrmWindowHost::IsVisible() const {
-  NOTREACHED();
+  return visible_;
 }
 
 void DrmWindowHost::PrepareForShutdown() {}
@@ -90,13 +94,21 @@ gfx::Rect DrmWindowHost::GetBoundsInPixels() const {
 }
 
 void DrmWindowHost::SetBoundsInDIP(const gfx::Rect& bounds) {
-  // No scaling at DRM level and should always use pixel bounds.
-  NOTREACHED();
+  // Upstream is NOTREACHED() here, on the premise that DRM does no scaling and
+  // callers should always use pixel bounds. That holds on ChromeOS, where ash
+  // never routes a window through DesktopWindowTreeHostPlatform. A views
+  // browser on Linux does, during WindowTreeHost::InitHost(), so the premise is
+  // false off ChromeOS and the NOTREACHED() is a crash on startup.
+  //
+  // The delegate is what knows the scale: PlatformWindowDelegate's own
+  // implementation is the identity, which is exactly the old premise, and
+  // DesktopWindowTreeHostPlatform overrides it with the real factor. So this
+  // preserves upstream behaviour wherever the premise really did hold.
+  SetBoundsInPixels(delegate_->ConvertRectToPixels(bounds));
 }
 
 gfx::Rect DrmWindowHost::GetBoundsInDIP() const {
-  // No scaling at DRM level and should always use pixel bounds.
-  NOTREACHED();
+  return delegate_->ConvertRectToDIP(bounds_);
 }
 
 void DrmWindowHost::SetTitle(const std::u16string& title) {}
@@ -161,20 +173,24 @@ void DrmWindowHost::ConfineCursorToBounds(const gfx::Rect& bounds) {
 }
 
 void DrmWindowHost::SetRestoredBoundsInDIP(const gfx::Rect& bounds) {
-  NOTREACHED();
+  restored_bounds_ = delegate_->ConvertRectToPixels(bounds);
 }
 
 gfx::Rect DrmWindowHost::GetRestoredBoundsInDIP() const {
-  NOTREACHED();
+  // Falls back to the current bounds, which is what a window that has never
+  // been maximised should restore to.
+  return delegate_->ConvertRectToDIP(restored_bounds_.value_or(bounds_));
 }
 
 void DrmWindowHost::SetWindowIcons(const gfx::ImageSkia& window_icon,
                                    const gfx::ImageSkia& app_icon) {
-  NOTREACHED();
+  // Nothing draws a titlebar on a CRTC, so there is nowhere to put an icon.
+  // Headless answers the same way, and for the same reason.
 }
 
 void DrmWindowHost::SizeConstraintsChanged() {
-  NOTREACHED();
+  // A window that fills a CRTC has no constraints to renegotiate. Reached
+  // during startup from DesktopNativeWidgetAura::InitNativeWidget().
 }
 
 void DrmWindowHost::OnCursorUpdate() {
diff --git a/ui/ozone/platform/drm/host/drm_window_host.h b/ui/ozone/platform/drm/host/drm_window_host.h
index 1d9a66f641da8..3250e6b7c9c23 100644
--- a/ui/ozone/platform/drm/host/drm_window_host.h
+++ b/ui/ozone/platform/drm/host/drm_window_host.h
@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@
 #include <stdint.h>
 
 #include <memory>
+#include <optional>
 
 #include "base/memory/raw_ptr.h"
 #include "ui/display/types/display_snapshot.h"
@@ -117,6 +118,12 @@ class DrmWindowHost : public PlatformWindow,
   const gfx::AcceleratedWidget widget_;
 
   gfx::Rect cursor_confined_bounds_;
+
+  // Domicile's engine fork. Upstream NOTREACHED()s the seven PlatformWindow
+  // methods a views browser asks for during startup, because ash never asks
+  // them on ChromeOS. These are what two of the answers need.
+  bool visible_ = false;
+  std::optional<gfx::Rect> restored_bounds_;
 };
 
 }  // namespace ui
